# STIG RHEL-09-653015: systemd auditd.service
# STIG ID: V-258152 (MEDIUM)

META
    esp_id `r9-rhel-09-653015-auditd-service-001`
    version `1.0.0`
    dsl_schema_version `1.0.0`
    platform `rocky9`
    criticality `high`

    title `STIG RHEL-09-653015: RHEL 9 audit service must be enabled.`
    description `RHEL 9 audit service must be enabled.`
    author `example-security`
    tags `rhel9,stig,disa-stig,service,systemd`

    control_mapping `DISA-STIG:RHEL-09-653015,NIST-800-53:AU-12,NIST-800-53:AU-12(3),NIST-800-53:AU-14(1),NIST-800-53:AU-3,NIST-800-53:AU-3(1),NIST-800-53:AU-6(4),NIST-800-53:AU-7,NIST-800-53:AU-7(1),NIST-800-53:AU-8,NIST-800-53:CM-5(1)(B),NIST-800-53:MA-3(5),NIST-800-53:MA-4(1)(A)`
    control_objective `AU-12`

    assessment_method `TEST`
    implementation_status `implemented`
    responsible_role `system-admin`

    control_origination `sp-system`
    inherited_from `Rocky9:localhost:os-hardening`
    customer_responsibility `configuration`

    remediation_days `30`
    recommendation `Review and remediate per DISA STIG guidance for RHEL-09-653015.`

    component_id `comp-r9-os`

    impl_AU_12 `This control is validated by checking the required system configuration against the DISA STIG baseline for RHEL 9.`

META_END

DEF
    OBJECT svc_check
        unit_name `auditd.service`
    OBJECT_END

    STATE svc_state
        found boolean = true
        active_state string = `active`
        enabled string = `enabled`
    STATE_END

    CRI AND
        CTN systemd_service
            TEST all all AND
            STATE_REF svc_state
            OBJECT_REF svc_check
        CTN_END
    CRI_END
DEF_END
